 1161 003140             ! ------------------------------------------------------------
 1162 003140             ! SICLOSE -- v0.10h5 SII-specific interface cleanup.
 1163 003140             !
 1164 003140             ! Hardware test result:
 1165 003140             !
 1166 003140             !       CONTROL <select-code>,16;2
 1167 003140             !
 1168 003140             ! reliably repairs every observed post-PRTSCREEN failure.  Therefore restore
 1169 003140             ! CR16 directly and immediately after the final SII HPOUT has completed.
 1170 003140             !
Page   21                                                             
CAPASM

 1171 003140             ! IMPORTANT: HPIB7 is generic.  It derives the translator register pair from
 1172 003140             ! PSCODE, which was decoded from the first PRTSCREEN argument.  No select
 1173 003140             ! code is hardcoded here.
 1174 003140             !
 1175 003140             ! Do NOT send the old explicit 077-octal UNLISTEN in the SII path.  In failing
 1176 003140             ! v0.10h3 runs that value was seen by the printer as ASCII '?' (decimal 63),
 1177 003140             ! indicating that the command could escape as peripheral data.
 1178 003140             ! ------------------------------------------------------------
 1179 003140             
 1180 003140 230         SICLOSE BIN
 1181 003141 114 261 233         LDMD R14,=BINTAB
      003144 202 
 1182 003145             
 1183 003145             ! EBTKS settling delay.  Physical testing proved that BASIC
 1184 003145             !     CONTROL <select-code>,16;2
 1185 003145             ! always repairs the virtual HP-IB interface.  v0.10h5/v0.10i1 made this
 1186 003145             ! substantially more reliable by delaying the assembler-side CR16 restore,
 1187 003145             ! but one residual text-corruption case remained.  v0.10i2 therefore uses a
 1188 003145             ! longer initial quiet interval and performs the CR16=2 write twice, with a
 1189 003145             ! shorter quiet interval between writes and again before returning to BASIC.
 1190 003145             !
 1191 003145             ! All delays are CPU-only.  Generic HPIB7 is called immediately before each
 1192 003145             ! HPCTRL so the translator always comes from PSCODE decoded from PRTSCREEN's
 1193 003145             ! first parameter; no select code is hardcoded here.
 1194 003145             
